From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:15:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jpegparse: Take the container height only for interlaced
 fields

The caps height was taken from the container whenever it was larger
than the height of the image, to report the frame height of interlaced
MJPEG whose images are fields. That also hit a resolution change in the
middle of a stream: a Matroska MJPEG track declared 640x480 whose images
switch to 320x240 got caps of 320x480 with interlace-mode progressive.
jpegdec, which takes an image of half the caps height for a field, then
output nothing for the images after the switch, while decoders that
parse the image themselves were not affected.

Use the container height only when the stream was found interlaced, and
take a smaller first image for a field only when it has the width of the
frame: a field is half the frame height at the full frame width.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 gst/jpegformat/gstjpegparse.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gst/jpegformat/gstjpegparse.c b/gst/jpegformat/gstjpegparse.c
index f76d136..48c7b9b 100644
--- a/gst/jpegformat/gstjpegparse.c
+++ b/gst/jpegformat/gstjpegparse.c
@@ -579,7 +579,9 @@ gst_jpeg_parse_sof (GstJpegParse * parse, GstJpegSegment * seg)
         sizeof (parse->sampling_factors));
 
     if (parse->first_picture && !parse->multiscope) {
+      /* A field has the width of the frame and about half of its height. */
       if (parse->orig_height > 0
+          && (parse->orig_width == 0 || parse->orig_width == hdr.width)
           && parse->height < ((parse->orig_height * 3) / 4)) {
         parse->interlace_mode = GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_INTERLEAVED;
       } else if (parse->avid) {
@@ -1201,7 +1203,11 @@ gst_jpeg_parse_set_new_caps (GstJpegParse * parse)
 
   if (parse->width > 0)
     gst_caps_set_simple (caps, "width", G_TYPE_INT, parse->width, NULL);
-  if (parse->orig_height > 0 && parse->orig_height > parse->height)
+  /* Interlaced MJPEG: every image is a field and the caps carry the frame
+   * height of the container. Otherwise the image size is the picture size,
+   * whatever the container said (the resolution may change mid-stream). */
+  if (parse->interlace_mode == GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_INTERLEAVED
+      && parse->orig_height > parse->height)
     gst_caps_set_simple (caps, "height", G_TYPE_INT, parse->orig_height, NULL);
   else if (parse->height > 0)
     gst_caps_set_simple (caps, "height", G_TYPE_INT, parse->height, NULL);
